- **$2 \mid v_2 - v_0$** and **$2 \mid v_3 - v_1$**: So $v_2 \equiv v_0 \pmod{2}$ and $v_3 \equiv v_1 \pmod{2}$.
- **$3 \mid v_4 - v_1$**: So $v_4 \equiv v_1 \pmod{3}$.

